<mujoco model="wx200_mjwarp_scene">
  <!--
    The scene the batched MJWarp backend loads for this arm: the robot and room
    from `wx200_scene.xml` plus the CDPR's four fixed-topology object slots,
    included rather than copied.

    The slot file is embodiment-independent by design (four free bodies, one
    visual mesh and eleven primitive colliders each), so sharing the one copy
    keeps the two embodiments' slot names, collider classes, and park poses
    identical - which is what lets the collector, the rewards, and the success
    predicates run on either robot unedited. Its asset paths
    (`../../../assets/externals/robocasa/...`) resolve from this directory to
    the same repository root as from the CDPR's, because both scene files sit
    three levels below it. That is also why `wx200.xml` names its meshes as
    `meshes/...` rather than through a `meshdir`: a compiler meshdir would apply
    to the RoboCasa meshes too and send them to the wrong place.

    Object SIZES are not set here. `cdpr_object_catalog` rescales every visual
    mesh and primitive collider for this gripper's 8-52 mm span when
    RLVLA_EMBODIMENT=widowx200, at compile time, so the XML stays shared.
  -->
  <include file="wx200_scene.xml"/>
  <include file="../../cdpr/cdpr_mujoco/cdpr_mjwarp_object_slots.xml"/>
</mujoco>
